 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your fence needs posts, so you dig a shallow hole and push one in. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the wind pushes on the fence, and the short post tips right over.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you bury about a third of the post's length in the ground.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But a few years later, the wood rots right at the ground line, and it snaps.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "That's where the wood stays wet and still gets air. Perfect food for fungus.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you set the post in concrete.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But rain runs down the post and gets trapped in the concrete cup. It rots anyway.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you put gravel at the bottom of the hole, so the water drains away.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And you use pressure treated wood, soaked with chemicals that fungus can't eat.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a fence that lasts. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
